WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.968
-Now, it is the end of the week,
and that's usually when

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.133
I catch up with
some personal stuff.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.667
I check my inbox,
I return emails,

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.334
and of course, I send out
thank you notes.

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:08.501
So, I was just wondering,
can I --

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:09.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.000
Thank you so much.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.067
I would like to write out
some thank you notes right now.

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:15.234
James, can I get some thank you
note writing music, please?

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.467
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.300
It always works better when
you turn your keyboard on.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.133
Always sounds better when you
turn the keyboard on, yeah.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:35.334
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.167
Thank you, Snoop Dogg,

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.834
for releasing
THC-infused Funyuns.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.167
Though, if you're
eating Funyuns,

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.667
you're probably
already THC-infused.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.234
That's -- Yeah, I just wonder...

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:49.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:55.834
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.501
Thank you, cauldrons,

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.834
for meaning you're about to get
one of two things --

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.067
a deadly potion,

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.567
or tableside guac.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:03.734
Oh, yeah.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.567
Yeah. Cool.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.567
[ Applause ]

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.634
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:14.801
Thank you, Meta's new
Quest Pro VR headset,

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:17.534
for making everyone look like
my grandma in Boca Raton.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:19.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.667
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:29.501
Thank you, juice press
in my kitchen,

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.667
for letting everyone know
there was one day last year

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.667
when I thought
I'd get into juicing.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.834
"I'm gonna do this every day.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.334
I'm gonna do this every day."

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.367
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.634
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.467
Thank you, trick-or-treating,

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:48.801
for being the only time you can
knock on a stranger's door,

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.133
vaguely threaten them,

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.634
and expect candy in return.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:53.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.067
[ Keyboard playing ]

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:04.234
Thank you, opening a bottle
of wine alone,

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.167
for being no problem whatsoever.

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:08.734
And thank you,
opening a bottle of wine

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.000
in front of other people,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.968
for being the most stressful
moment of my life.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:15.467
There you have it, everyone.
Those are my thank you notes.

